      "pid": 931604,
      "tid": 122647,
      "content": "<p dir=\"auto\">I have been using Vivaldi Mail and Calendar on Linux for some time, alongside Betterbird.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One major limitation currently prevents me from switching to Vivaldi Mail permanently: the Contacts Panel does not display all the information stored in my contacts.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My contacts are maintained in Betterbird and synchronized via CardDAV with the Vivaldi server (<a href=\"http://calendar.vivaldi.net\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">calendar.vivaldi.net</a>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The synchronization itself works correctly. All contact information is also displayed correctly in Vivaldi Webmail.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, the integrated Contacts Panel in the Vivaldi browser does not display many of these details, including additional email addresses and other contact information.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For users with more comprehensive address books, this is a significant limitation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My questions to the Vivaldi development team:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Is this a known limitation or a bug in the Contacts Panel?</li>\n<li>Is full support for displaying and editing vCard contact fields planned?</li>\n<li>Are there plans to improve the Contacts Panel so that it can serve as a fully-fledged contact management solution?</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I would appreciate clarification on whether a substantial improvement is planned for a future Vivaldi release.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thank you<br />\nRW</p>\n",
